(function()
	_G.pg.base.task_data_template[23029] = {
		name = "Raise any shipgirl to Level 40.",
		guild_coin_award = 0,
		award = 0,
		type = 17,
		desc = "You can check the stats of your shipgirls by going from the home screen to \"Dock\", then tapping on a shipgirl to view her Info page. The stats you will see have the following effects:\nHP: Determines how much damage the ship can take in battle.\nFP: Increases the amount of damage the ship can deal with artillery and cannon-based attacks.\nAA: Increases the amount of damage the ship can deal with Anti-Air guns.\nArmor Type: Indicates the thickness of the ship's armor, which can be one of 3 types: Light, Medium, or Heavy. Each weapon has a different effectiveness against each armor type, so carefully consider the combination of ships and gear to bring to each battle to maximize your fleet's effectiveness.\nTRP: Increases the amount of damage the ship can deal with torpedo attacks.\nAVI: Increases the amount of damage dealt with aircraft.\nRLD: Affects the reload time of some gears.\nEVA: Affects the ship's chance to dodge and the likelihood of being critically hit.\nACC: Affects the ship's chance to land hits and the likelihood of dealing a critical hit.\nSPD: Affects the movement speed of the fleet during combat. In certain stages, also influences the number of tiles that the fleet can move per action.\nCost: Indicates the amount of Oil consumed by the ship per battle.\nASW: Increases the amount of damage the ship can deal with Anti-Sub weapons. Also affects sonar detection range.\nOXY: Affects the boat's maximum dive time. When a boat is submerged, the Oxygen gauge will be continuously depleted. When this gauge is emptied, the boat will be forced to surface.\nAMO: Determines how many times a Sub Fleet can attack and/or provide support.\nASR: Influences the range that the Sub Fleet can operate in. Sub fleets can be toggled between standy and search-and-destroy mode.\nIn search-and-destroy mode, sub fleets will automatically seek out enemies within their attack/support range and deplete a portion of their Max HP.\nLCK: A stat influenced by a shipgirl's historical record as well as the fate written in her hull. Has a subtle influence on many aspects of battle.\nMorale: Reflects the willingness of a shipgirl to sortie. Shipgirls with high morale will receive bonus EXP from sorties, whereas sortieing a shipgirl with low morale will cause her to receive halved EXP, as well as causing her Affinity to decrease.\nPower: A general evaluation of the shipgirl's combat readiness, based on the combined value of her gear, stats, and other factors.",
		count_inherit = 0,
		sub_type = 1017,
